Date: Mon, 6 Sep 93 01:52:04 -0700
From: dasher@netcom.com (D. Anton Sherwood)
Subject: Vinge shares Hugo award for best novel

The Hugo awards banquet ended about three hours ago.  (The Hugos, in case some
of you may not know, are voted by members of the World Science Fiction
Convention.)  Votes for Best Novel were tied between DOOMSDAY BOOK, by
Connie Willis, and A FIRE UPON THE DEEP, by Vernor Vinge.  I find this
quite a satisfying result.  Vinge explores the vital (to Extropians)
themes of mind and identity, reputation and deceit, with great insight--
but in a plot that many readers found deeply flawed; Willis gives us an
equally thick but better crafted story of what used to be called Christian
love (and time travel and the plague).

I salute both co-winners.

